#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
batch_films_modern_1.py — v7.110

Grows the Films deck from ~460 to ~800 topics with modern Hollywood
crowd-pleasers (2000–2025): fun, good, worth-watching movies with proper
facts and personalized watch instructions. This is the durable CONTENT fix
the pickFrom() AGENT NOTE (v7.94) called for — the recency weight only
balances the odds; more modern tier-1 topics are the real cure.

Entry format (tuple):
  (title, year, director, genre1, genre2, runtime_min, tier, teaser, instruction)

Rules enforced here (mirrors the films.json schema + validate_topics):
  - Dedupes against the existing films.json by normalized title.
  - id = "film-{kebab-slug}-{year}", made unique with a -N suffix if taken.
  - name = "Title (Year)" (<= 80 chars).
  - teaser <= 450 chars — the "one quirky fact" angle, NOT a Wikipedia bio.
  - instruction <= 450 chars — personalized watch guidance.
  - tags = [genre1, genre2, "{decade}s", "Hollywood"].
  - byline = director.
  - exploreAction = Watch "{Title (Year)} end-to-end" · runtime · instruction.
  - tier: 1 = marquee crowd-pleaser, 2 = good but slightly more niche.

Usage: python3 scripts/batch_films_modern_1.py   (run from repo root)
Then:   python3 scripts/validate_topics.py
"""

